{"id": "10th-u2-q132", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "single_choice", "level": "standard", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "10", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_2", "lesson_id": "thogainilai_thodargal", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "vetrumai_urubugal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தமிழ் இலக்கணத்தில் வேற்றுமை உருபுகள் இல்லாத முதல் மற்றும் எட்டாம் வேற்றுமைகள் முறையே எவ்வாறு அழைக்கப்படும்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "செயப்படுபொருள் வேற்றுமை, கருவி வேற்றுமை", "B": "கொடை வேற்றுமை, எல்லை வேற்றுமை", "C": "கிழமை வேற்றுமை, இட வேற்றுமை", "D": "எழுவாய் வேற்றுமை, விளி வேற்றுமை"}, "explanation": "முதல் வேற்றுமை \"எழுவாய் வேற்றுமை\" என்றும், எட்டாம் வேற்றுமை \"விளி வேற்றுமை\" என்றும் அழைக்கப்படும். இவ்விரண்டிற்கும் வேற்றுமை உருபுகள் இல்லை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "What are the 1st and 8th cases (which possess no case markers) designated as in Tamil grammar?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Accusative, Instrumental", "B": "Dative, Ablative", "C": "Genitive, Locative", "D": "Nominative (Ezhuvai) and Vocative (Vili)"}, "explanation": "Case 1 is Ezhuvai (Nominative) and Case 8 is Vili (Vocative); neither takes internal case suffixes."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "10", "term": "full_